/-!
# Recovery and linearity of the original family Fourier series

The literal Fourier synthesis recovers its original Haar coefficients, and
the actual coefficients reconstruct every original smooth family. Equal
series are equivalent to equal coefficients on the given base. Addition,
finite sums, subtraction, and multiplication by a base scalar commute with
this same pointwise series. This package asserts neither joint smoothness
of general synthesized coefficients nor relative cohomological generation.
-/
